# Matched local reservoirs for unequal onsite gaps

Proposed conditional extension; not independently checked or accepted. Root's
construction uses the accepted local conserving schedule, its sparse
single-system-qubit implementation and the explicit driven sine preparation.
It is a driven laboratory construction with supplied control and preparation
permissions, not a native or autonomous physical identification.

## 1. Actual generator, geometry and target interface

Let q>=1 and let the actual old register S have

    K_S = E0 I + sum_(i=1)^q Delta_i n_(S_i),
    E0>=0, Delta_i>0, n=|1><1|.

The positive gaps need not be equal, rationally related or nondegenerate.
They are physical parameters supplied with computable enclosures when an
effective numerical schedule is requested. No old interaction is present.
The theorem does not remove or refocus an interacting old term.

At old site S_i attach a private branch B_i of M_i=L_i+2 qubits and a terminal
synthesis ancilla A_i, L_i>=1. Every qubit on this branch has gap Delta_i.
Write m_i=M_i+2=L_i+4 for its total sites, including S_i and A_i, and

    N_i = n_(S_i)+N_(B_i)+n_(A_i),
    F = E0 I + sum_i Delta_i N_i.

The q old sites form a supplied nearest-neighbour path; their private branches
are disjoint. This comb graph has degree at most three and, for example,
embeds with S_i=(i,0), B_i/A_i along the positive vertical ray. All other
bonds are zero in the stipulated controlled Hamiltonian. Existence of these
free sites and independently addressable edges is a premise, not a conclusion
about a fixed occupied lattice.

Available runtime controls are the accepted positive exchange/onsite-Z/full
SWAP generators along each equal-gap private branch, and

    Q_CZ = pi n_(S_i) n_(S_(i+1))

on adjacent old sites. The latter is positive, has norm pi and exponential
exp(-i Q_CZ)=CZ, with scalar one. Every permitted runtime generator commutes
with every N_i. The old register retains precisely K_S with coefficient one.
A physical full SWAP between unequal-gap old sites is NOT a permission:
[Delta_i n_i+Delta_j n_j,SWAP] is nonzero when Delta_i!=Delta_j.

First fix a finite chronological logical word P of arbitrary one-qubit
unitaries on S and adjacent CZ gates. Its full matrix, including its global
phase, is V. Let R_i count one-qubit gates on site i and R_CZ count CZs.
This explicit word is a classical input; requested complexity below is
conditional on it. Arbitrary unitary targets admit such finite words by the
usual one-qubit/CNOT universality theorem, CNOT=(I tensor H)CZ(I tensor H),
and logical SWAP=CNOT_12 CNOT_21 CNOT_12 for routing. This is an existence
corollary. No efficient classical matrix-to-word algorithm, uniform
computable-real branch selection or particular q-dependent decomposition
bound is inferred here. In particular, a resource bound with fixed R_i does
not automatically cover a target-approximation word whose length grows
with requested accuracy.

Primary attribution for this universality premise:
Barenco et al., Elementary gates for quantum computation,
https://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/9503016,
https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevA.52.3457.
The local construction below does not import their physical implementation.

## 2. Complete block semantics and a shared reservoir through a word

For branch i let |r> denote the M_i-qubit prefix string of weight r,
0<=r<=M_i. On S_i B_i, for every a_i=1,...,M_i, define the isometry

    J_(i,a_i)|x_i> = |x_i> |a_i-x_i>,  x_i in {0,1}.

Its two columns have the same N_i=a_i when A_i=0. Define the full
one-qubit lift ell_i(U) as U on every such pair and identity on its complete
orthogonal complement, including nonprefix strings and incomplete sectors.
This is exactly the accepted author's q=1, M_i=L_i+2 finite lift.
It is a unitary on every physical S_i B_i input and conserves their number.

For a=(a_1,...,a_q) with each a_i in 1,...,M_i, set J_a=tensor_i J_(i,a_i)
with the old logical factors ordered 1,...,q. The complete-subspace
projector P_full=sum_a J_a J_a* is preserved by each lifted one-qubit gate.
Furthermore, a physical old CZ satisfies

    CZ_(S_i,S_(i+1)) J_a = J_a CZ_(i,i+1).

This follows on every old bit string x from its phase (-1)^(x_i x_(i+1));
the reservoirs' prefix lengths do not enter that phase. Consequently the
full physical word C_P obtained by replacing each one-qubit letter U by
ell_i(U), and keeping the physical CZs, satisfies

    C_P J_a = J_a V                      (all complete a).

Each factor is a full physical unitary. C_P is defined on the whole Hilbert
space and commutes with every N_i. Its action on the complement of P_full
is the actual product of those factors; it is NOT asserted to be identity
there. In particular a physical CZ also acts on nonprefix inputs. No
unjustified full-space homomorphism or discarded off-code extension is used.

This identity holds for any word length using the SAME branch reservoirs.
No fresh state or reset is inserted between logical gates. Logical routing
between unequal-gap old sites is implemented by the lifted CNOT word;
it is not the forbidden physical old-site SWAP. The fuel changes balance
each species charge separately, so unequal old-energy transfers remain
compatible with conservation of the total F.

## 3. Joint packet approximation independent of logical word length

Supply independent branch packets

    beta_i = sum_(l=1)^L_i b_(i,l)|l>,
    b_(i,l)=sqrt(2/(L_i+1)) sin(pi l/(L_i+1)),
    beta=tensor_i beta_i,

and independent A_i=0, retaining every old/battery/ancilla/reference output.
For every old input, beta places a_i=x_i+l in 1,...,L_i+1, within the
complete a_i range. Thus the identity in section 2 applies to the whole
input isometry, not merely a selected pure old state.

Here is a direct vector estimate, without summing an error per letter.
Temporarily identify each prefix-count coordinate with the corresponding
subset of ell^2(Z) and extend beta_i by zero. Let T_i be unit translation
and put

    D = sum_x |x><x| tensor product_i T_i^(-x_i).

On the supported complete block inputs C_P equals
D(V tensor I)D*. The conjugation shifts the ith battery count by
x_i-y_i for a matrix element |y><x|, which is just the fixed-total-charge
rule in section 2. All counts that occur at the beginning or end lie
between zero and L_i+1, so the infinite translation notation imports no
physical wrap, leakage or unbounded reservoir.

Set d_i=||T_i beta_i-beta_i||=2 sin(pi/[2(L_i+1)]).
For every x, the tensor-product telescoping inequality gives

    ||(product_i T_i^(x_i)) beta-beta|| <= sum_i d_i.

Because D is diagonal in orthogonal old x blocks, this also bounds
||D* J_beta-J_beta|| and ||D J_beta-J_beta|| as operator norms on the
entire old input space. Applying the triangle inequality on the two sides
of V gives

    ||C_P J_beta-J_beta V|| <= 2 sum_i d_i.

The same norm estimate survives tensoring an arbitrary passive reference.
For arbitrary old/reference density inputs the unhalved complete trace
distance is at most

    4 sum_i d_i <= 4pi sum_i 1/(L_i+1).

The packet error depends on q and the chosen packet sizes, not R_i or
R_CZ. It is the finite-lift translation estimate applied to a physically
composable family, not a new general catalytic-resource principle.
The actual output may be correlated with the reservoirs. Reusing this
fixed finite register during a coherent word does not establish indefinite
reuse for successive fresh energy-demanding systems.

## 4. Actual local compilation, phases and ancilla reuse

For each one-qubit logical letter, use the accepted q=1 sparse conserving
