    C_(i,U) J_(A_i) = J_(A_i) ell_i(U)

with phase one. A numerical implementation may instead have a certified
full-isometry discrepancy eta_(i,U); if a scalar zeta is allowed by the
chosen certificate it must be explicitly carried through the word.
All S_i B_i inputs are covered. Thus one initially clean A_i can be used
throughout its branch's word: comparison with the exact clean-return
factors and unitary telescoping gives total vector compiler allowance
eta_C<=sum_letters eta_letter. Imperfect actual ancillas are never silently
reset. The complete initial readiness allowance covers all A_i jointly.

The exact sparse bound for a branch is

    n_i=L_i+3,
    Gbar_i=(2n_i-1)(L_i+2)152[T(n_i-2)+T(n_i-1)],
    T(1)=1, T(k)=2T(floor(k/2))+2T(ceil(k/2)),
    Gbar_i<=131328 L_i^4.

This counts all routed elementary A/Z/full-SWAP gates, including the
clean-ancilla determinant phase. The q=1 constant is the accepted K_q
formula at q=1. A one-qubit gate's determinant phase is relative to
its physical complement and cannot be discarded.

A serial implementation of the whole logical word therefore has

    G <= Gbar_total = R_CZ + sum_i R_i Gbar_i.

Pad to this integer bound if a target-independent duration for this fixed
