eta_H=(1/hbar) integral_0^tau ||H_actual(t)-H_nominal(t)||dt.
If sampling occurs after all pulses are off, a timing allowance may use
eta_t=||F|| |delta_t|/hbar, with the actual post-off F specified.
Then the complete endpoint trace error is at most

    e_out <= epsilon_ready + 4 sum_i d_i + 2eta_C+2eta_H+2eta_t.

If a supplied finite target word approximates a desired V in operator
