## 6. Explicit driven preparation on the same graph

On branch i the accepted preparation with q=1 uses L_i serial rotations:
one positive Y flip followed by L_i-1 conditional rotations. Use
2pi I+(pi/2)Y for the flip and n_control(2pi I+theta Y) for each edge,
with the accepted sine-tail angles. These are onsite or adjacent branch
controls. Their reserves exponentiate to identity on the complete local
spaces. They are number-changing controls and are an EXTRA preparation
permission, not supplied by the conserving runtime alphabet.

Prepare branches sequentially in a declared global time coordinate, with
G_p=sum_i L_i rotation slots. On branch i use the laboratory carrier

    hbar f_(h_p)(t-t_j) exp(-it H_(B_i)/hbar) Q exp(it H_(B_i)/hbar),
    H_(B_i)=Delta_i N_(B_i).

All old degrees remain decoupled during preparation and retain K_S.
The interaction-picture circuit produces tensor_i beta_i independently of
their preparation order. An already prepared branch continues freely
while other branches are acted on; that phase is NOT dropped.
Choose one common duration using Delta_max:

    h_p >= max(4hbar Q*/g, sqrt(8pi hbar Q*/sigma),
                                           4pi Delta_max/sigma).

Then tau_p=(G_p+1)h_p is fixed. The last slot applies species-specific
lambda_(p,i) n simultaneously to every BATTERY site, computed from the
complete tau_p by the same enclosure rule. It cancels all branch free
aging including waiting while other branches were prepared. Ancillas remain
in independent vacuum. The exact full input isometry is

    U_prep J_vac = J_beta exp(-i tau_p K_S/hbar).

To act as V on the original old input, implement W=V exp(i tau_p K_S/hbar)
in runtime. The right factor is a product of known onsite old phases
and the scalar exp(iE0 tau_p/hbar); it may be included in a supplied logical
word, with its actual count and scalar retained. Then W exp(-i tau_p K_S/hbar)=V.
The vector comparator retains the runtime scalar gamma(W). Density
comparison has total error at most e_prep+e_runtime. No freshly reset
actual battery is inserted at the interface.

The product packet mean, variance bound and battery norm are

    mu_B=sum_i Delta_i (L_i+1)/2,
    Var_B<=sum_i Delta_i^2 (L_i-1)^2/4,
    ||H_B||=sum_i M_i Delta_i.

The variance sum uses the nominal independent product packet, not arbitrary
actual correlated output. Preparation's ideal modeled net work is mu_B.
An absolute-work bound is
g(G_p+sum_i M_i)+(pi/2)sum_i Delta_i L_i.
Each carrier derivative is paid, and the final phases change no number.
For joint preparation trace error e, mean/second-moment errors use the
