## 7. Existing scope and decisive review obligations

The existing finite energy-lift theorem already covers abstract finite
energy lists and their sine resources. This proposal's intended contribution
is a concrete bounded-degree, positive two-body driven schedule with
unequal onsite gaps, exact composition on the shared complete subspace,
separate final species phases, and compatible driven preparation.
It is not a new abstract lift theorem.

The existing onsite autonomous controller is a different supplied static
route; the existing interacting-controller history application retains
whole-chain copies and higher-body support. Their existence is not being
denied or republished. This proposal does not claim a generic interacting
two-body reduction or single-port access.

Load-bearing independent checks are: the complete-block action of physical
CZ and actual complement action; the word-independent translation bound;
legal branch-only routing and all ancilla reuse; q=1 sparse count and
global phase; species-dependent final cancellation while K stays installed;
old aging through sequential preparation; actual-error and moment ledgers.
A useful small discriminator is a two-species entangling word with
Delta_1=1, Delta_2=sqrt(2), including all selected charge blocks and a
wrong physical unequal-gap SWAP mutant. No such new execution is claimed
in this initial proposal.

